+**And the script that builds the coverage scan has moved ahead of them (noted 2026-09-09).** As
+committed today, `coverage_scan.py` defines its class I panel as `PANEL_AB + PANEL_C` — 34 HLA-A
+and HLA-B alleles plus 18 HLA-C alleles, 52 in all — while every artifact it and its consumers
+wrote records 34, HLA-A and HLA-B only. The committed 34 is element-for-element the script's
+current `PANEL_AB`, so the divergence is exactly the appended HLA-C block and nothing else. Its
+consequence is nonetheless that re-running the script today would not reproduce a single committed
+panel figure: `epitope-allele-matrix.json`, `epitope-allele-loose-matrix.json` and
+`epitope-allele-matrix-mhcnuggets.json` would record a 52-allele panel, `coverage-curve.json` a
+`panel_size` of 52, `predictor-concordance.json` an `n_panel` of 52 and
+`vaccine-threshold-calibration.json` a 52-allele decoy null over 90,480 rather than 59,160
+peptide-allele tests, and the 34-allele statements in Sections 2.2, 2.3, 7, B1, B4, the Figure 2
+caption and Table 2 would each have to be restated. Table 2's generator would need an HLA-C row
+before it could render such a panel at all: it emits HLA-A and HLA-B rows only, so it would head
+the table 52 while listing 34. Which of the two changed first cannot be established from the
+history — the script and all of the artifacts arrive in one squashed merge — so no ordering is
+asserted here.
+
+This withdraws nothing that this paper reports. The figures are the record of the run that produced
+them, on the 34-allele panel Table 2 lists, and they are pinned to those committed artifacts rather
+than to a re-execution of the current script; Section 8 should not be read as promising the second.
+What a 52-allele run would give is left open in size and closed in sign. The size is UNKNOWN: no
+HLA-C allele frequency is present in this project's frequency source, and none was obtained for
+this note, so how far a coverage figure would move cannot be computed and is not guessed at. The
+sign is fixed by the arithmetic: alleles are only added to the panel, each allele is scored as its
+own single-allele sample so no existing call is disturbed, and coverage accumulates as
+1 − ∏(1 − af)², which is non-decreasing. A re-run can therefore raise a coverage figure or leave it
+unchanged, and cannot lower one.
+
